1
00:00:09,467 --> 00:00:11,053
If we give him what he wants...

2
00:00:11,136 --> 00:00:15,182
If we give Usher what he says,
his justice, that is it.

3
00:00:15,265 --> 00:00:17,267
It's over. He owns us.

4
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:20,228
- Don't exaggerate.
- I wish I were.

5
00:00:20,312 --> 00:00:23,440
- You've made a thousand deals.
- Yeah, well, this one is different.

6
00:00:23,523 --> 00:00:26,484
- Why?
- Because I can feel it right here.

7
00:00:26,569 --> 00:00:28,821
- Do you hear yourself?
- Yeah, loud and clear.

8
00:00:28,904 --> 00:00:32,866
I'm a little confused that you
don't seem to hear me at all.

9
00:00:32,950 --> 00:00:34,868
Once we're solidly back in power,

10
00:00:34,952 --> 00:00:36,870
- we will regain our position...
- That is naive.

11
00:00:36,954 --> 00:00:38,872
Naive is new for you.

12
00:00:38,956 --> 00:00:40,749
Realistic. Not naive.

13
00:00:40,833 --> 00:00:42,960
Everything we've worked for,
we can kiss it goodbye.

14
00:00:43,043 --> 00:00:45,503
We agreed to Usher's pick.
It's non-negotiable.

15
00:00:45,588 --> 00:00:49,341
That's exactly right. It's his pick.
It's his justice.

16
00:00:49,424 --> 00:00:52,595
He's trying to control our house.
The White House.

17
00:00:52,678 --> 00:00:55,055
I gave him my word, Francis.

18
00:00:56,431 --> 00:00:57,432
Your word?

19
00:00:58,559 --> 00:01:02,187
Your word? This
conversation is pointless.

20
00:01:02,270 --> 00:01:03,521
Grow up!

21
00:01:04,815 --> 00:01:05,816
Who do you think you are?

22
00:01:05,899 --> 00:01:09,527
I think I am a temporary president
trying to get you back in office.

23
00:01:09,612 --> 00:01:12,615
And if you don't think that we're
at a critical juncture in the road,

24
00:01:12,698 --> 00:01:15,075
you are pathetically mistaken.

25
00:01:15,158 --> 00:01:17,620
Wake up, Claire! Wake up!

26
00:03:13,902 --> 00:03:17,865
Recorded this morning EET in the
Yarmouk neighborhood of Damascus.

27
00:03:22,702 --> 00:03:25,998
Seems he developed a taste for
chocolate while at Cambridge.

28
00:03:27,249 --> 00:03:30,919
Smiling for the camera is Ahmed
Al Ahmadi, Yusuf's brother.

29
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:34,297
Are you sure?

30
00:03:34,381 --> 00:03:39,094
I had a long conversation with Yusuf
Al Ahmadi. They look nothing alike.

31
00:03:39,177 --> 00:03:40,303
It's him.

32
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:44,224
Is Ahmed still in our sights?

33
00:03:44,307 --> 00:03:46,894
- He is.
- This is a rare opportunity.

34
00:03:46,977 --> 00:03:48,937
We should seize the moment
and make a targeted strike.

35
00:03:49,021 --> 00:03:50,898
- Director, please.
- Madam President...

36
00:03:50,981 --> 00:03:53,608
Is there some issue, General?

37
00:03:57,029 --> 00:03:59,114
Ahmed Al Ahmadi didn't
travel all the way

38
00:03:59,197 --> 00:04:01,658
from his compound to
Damascus to buy a candy bar.

39
00:04:01,742 --> 00:04:03,786
He's meeting with someone.
Let's find out who.

40
00:04:03,869 --> 00:04:06,997
Unless we're detected, and
he disappears for good.

41
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:10,542
But if we wait, there's a huge
potential to learn more about ICO.

42
00:04:11,015 --> 00:04:14,018
Its members, contacts, habits, tactics.

43
00:04:14,629 --> 00:04:17,299
You know, you're sounding
uncharacteristically dovish

44
00:04:17,382 --> 00:04:18,759
this morning, General.

45
00:04:21,011 --> 00:04:23,096
I agree with General Braegher.

46
00:04:23,180 --> 00:04:26,016
While a successful air
strike against Ahmadi

47
00:04:26,099 --> 00:04:28,880
- would play well...
- This isn't about the election, Cathy.

48
00:04:29,227 --> 00:04:32,439
No, of course not. I mean,
if we do this correctly,

49
00:04:32,522 --> 00:04:35,317
we can begin the process of
dismantling ICO's network.

50
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:36,318
Take him out.

51
00:04:38,189 --> 00:04:42,152
If the president agrees, I think
it's the best thing for the country.

52
00:04:42,991 --> 00:04:45,493
Well, I think it would send a
very clear message to ICO.

53
00:04:45,577 --> 00:04:49,664
- In the short term, yes, but...
- No other term is relevant.

54
00:04:53,113 --> 00:04:54,999
I think we have been operating under

55
00:04:55,024 --> 00:04:56,922
the shadow of terror for too long.

56
00:04:57,005 --> 00:04:59,757
For the sake of the American
people, we need to act now.

57
00:04:59,842 --> 00:05:01,330
What's the timetable, General?

58
00:05:01,927 --> 00:05:04,972
For an actionable location,
most likely a number of hours.

59
00:05:05,597 --> 00:05:06,639
Thank you.

60
00:05:09,009 --> 00:05:11,136
You're wasting our time.

61
00:05:11,161 --> 00:05:13,538
We're being selective about
where and how he appears.

62
00:05:13,563 --> 00:05:14,815
Soon he won't be at any events at all.

63
00:05:14,898 --> 00:05:17,234
We're just trying to land him
and you in the White House.

64
00:05:17,317 --> 00:05:21,613
And it's not Brockhart-Conway, Mark.
It's the opposite.

65
00:05:22,780 --> 00:05:25,533
- He won't put up with this much longer.
- I'm sure it's hard on him.

66
00:05:25,617 --> 00:05:28,703
- I have to take this. I'm sorry.
- What happens after he gets there?

67
00:05:28,786 --> 00:05:32,040
- To Will? What happens?
- We'll be there for him.

68
00:05:32,124 --> 00:05:34,126
- You and General Brockhart?
- Yes.

69
00:05:35,611 --> 00:05:37,821
What will Will's role be?

70
00:05:39,172 --> 00:05:41,174
I will continue to support your husband.

71
00:05:41,601 --> 00:05:45,145
Give me a real answer. You owe me that.

72
00:05:45,803 --> 00:05:49,057
His role will be President
of the United States.

73
00:05:53,504 --> 00:05:54,713
Hey.

74
00:05:57,482 --> 00:05:59,692
The mic was still hot and
Brockhart just kept talking.

75
00:05:59,776 --> 00:06:01,861
- That's what she said.
- Insubordination?

76
00:06:02,862 --> 00:06:05,657
- That's the word she used?
- It's what it sounded like to her.

77
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:08,994
He was talking about
soldiers and he said, quote,

78
00:06:09,077 --> 00:06:11,329
"I'll be the first to
tell them not to listen."

79
00:06:11,413 --> 00:06:13,671
Can she get her hands
on the actual clip?

80
00:06:13,683 --> 00:06:14,457
For a price.

81
00:06:14,541 --> 00:06:16,626
- I thought she was a friend.
- Yeah, a smart friend.

82
00:06:16,880 --> 00:06:19,304
It's a nice 30-second
spot, post-debate.

83
00:06:19,543 --> 00:06:20,903
If there is a debate.

84
00:06:22,132 --> 00:06:25,802
Hits them at their strength. Takes
the military credibility away.

85
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:29,889
This is the kind of thing
that can turn an election.

86
00:06:31,995 --> 00:06:36,458
Whatever this costs... it's worth it.

87
00:06:39,649 --> 00:06:41,318
Let's secure it and then verify it.

88
00:06:44,988 --> 00:06:48,033
Recess appointment of
Judge Benson or no,

89
00:06:48,116 --> 00:06:51,786
people need to stay focused on
the revote in Tennessee and Ohio

90
00:06:51,869 --> 00:06:53,121
and how the hell we got here.

91
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:54,831
All right.

92
00:06:55,748 --> 00:06:58,168
I'll have my assistant Angela reach out

93
00:06:58,251 --> 00:07:00,753
to confirm what time you
need me at the studio.

94
00:07:01,671 --> 00:07:05,175
All right. Yep. Yeah.

95
00:07:07,885 --> 00:07:09,715
I collected everything
I could find about

96
00:07:09,727 --> 00:07:11,306
the day Doug Stamper was carjacked.

97
00:07:11,389 --> 00:07:12,890
Good.

98
00:07:13,092 --> 00:07:14,759
All right, so...

99
00:07:16,228 --> 00:07:17,562
where was that?

100
00:07:19,814 --> 00:07:21,274
Where that happened?

101
00:07:22,567 --> 00:07:24,069
In Maryland.

102
00:07:25,070 --> 00:07:29,116
Right around, um...

103
00:07:29,199 --> 00:07:32,160
Yeah, I grew up about a
half an hour from there...

104
00:07:32,244 --> 00:07:34,121
It's here.

105
00:07:36,831 --> 00:07:39,459
And Rachel Posner's...

106
00:07:40,877 --> 00:07:43,588
last known address.

107
00:07:59,521 --> 00:08:01,898
I'd say they were
about 15 minutes apart.

108
00:08:08,338 --> 00:08:11,549
I'm not sure why I need
to explain myself to you.

109
00:08:11,574 --> 00:08:12,825
Why would you go to the NSA?

110
00:08:12,909 --> 00:08:16,746
I was inquiring into the
well-being of an American citizen.

111
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:19,208
He's just a disgruntled hacker.

112
00:08:19,220 --> 00:08:21,626
Then why are you so
interested in him?

113
00:08:24,504 --> 00:08:25,588
How did he look?

114
00:08:26,423 --> 00:08:27,882
I'm asking for me.

115
00:08:27,965 --> 00:08:30,097
I've known Aidan since
I was 13 years old.

116
00:08:30,109 --> 00:08:32,054
He and my mom dated for several years.

117
00:08:32,137 --> 00:08:33,305
Was a long time ago, obviously.

118
00:08:33,712 --> 00:08:36,548
But as far as the NSA
job, he didn't want it.

119
00:08:36,573 --> 00:08:38,032
I made him take it.

120
00:08:39,519 --> 00:08:43,940
I don't understand how they
got him or why he's there.

121
00:08:44,024 --> 00:08:46,109
I need to know that he is safe.

122
00:08:47,194 --> 00:08:48,653
He looked fine.

123
00:08:51,323 --> 00:08:52,907
What does he know, LeAnn?

124
00:08:53,575 --> 00:08:55,368
Probably about the same as you and me,

125
00:08:55,756 --> 00:08:59,343
which is why we need to keep him
out of any serious trouble.

126
00:09:04,836 --> 00:09:08,090
I don't want to get involved
in your personal life, LeAnn.

127
00:09:09,549 --> 00:09:11,384
- I'm here to see the president.
- Of course.

128
00:09:11,468 --> 00:09:14,471
But when you think about it, Cathy,
we're all sort of involved here.

129
00:09:15,388 --> 00:09:18,683
If he is in any kind of danger,
he is not built for it.

130
00:09:18,766 --> 00:09:20,017
Hi, Cathy.

131
00:09:20,935 --> 00:09:22,979
Jane.

132
00:09:24,856 --> 00:09:28,025
LeAnn Harvey, Jane Davis.
Jane is under secretary...

133
00:09:28,110 --> 00:09:30,382
Deputy under secretary of commerce for

134
00:09:30,394 --> 00:09:32,739
international trade. It's a mouthful.

135
00:09:32,822 --> 00:09:34,116
Yeah, it's good to put
a face to the voice.

136
00:09:35,158 --> 00:09:36,993
Uh, do you have any ibuprofen?

137
00:09:37,077 --> 00:09:38,953
- Oh, I might have some aspirin.
- No.

138
00:09:40,215 --> 00:09:43,092
- I'm allergic. Gives me hives.
- We may have some.

139
00:09:45,377 --> 00:09:48,838
You're the Harveys of
the tire company, yes?

140
00:09:51,341 --> 00:09:54,719
My father and uncle sold
the business 20 years ago.

141
00:09:54,802 --> 00:09:56,638
And the treads haven't
been the same since.

142
00:09:59,474 --> 00:10:01,934
But it's great. You
finally landed in D.C.

143
00:10:03,060 --> 00:10:04,771
I'll let the president
know you're both here.

144
00:10:05,041 --> 00:10:06,710
Uh, thank you for this.

145
00:10:12,404 --> 00:10:14,691
Uh, let's just reverse
those two sentences

146
00:10:14,703 --> 00:10:16,574
and it's there. It's to the point.

147
00:10:17,575 --> 00:10:20,495
- Pithy.
- Yes, pithy.

148
00:10:22,830 --> 00:10:24,332
Your meeting is here.

149
00:10:26,418 --> 00:10:28,128
Thank you.

150
00:10:28,211 --> 00:10:29,764
And Justice Benson is en route to the

151
00:10:29,776 --> 00:10:31,256
White House for the announcement.

152
00:10:31,339 --> 00:10:32,965
I'll have her wait in the Yellow Oval.

153
00:10:33,633 --> 00:10:35,927
Uh, great. Can you send
the others in, please?

154
00:10:36,306 --> 00:10:37,475
Of course.

155
00:10:39,472 --> 00:10:41,641
Is the former president meeting
us in the Rose Garden?

156
00:10:41,724 --> 00:10:43,310
Francis will not be there.

157
00:10:45,284 --> 00:10:46,285
He's not needed.

158
00:10:52,944 --> 00:10:54,111
Miss Davis.

159
00:10:54,696 --> 00:10:55,863
Secretary Durant.

160
00:10:58,074 --> 00:11:01,328
- It's been a long time.
- Yes, where was that?

161
00:11:01,411 --> 00:11:04,581
A think tank
in Aspen, early 2000.

162
00:11:04,664 --> 00:11:07,459
Oh, there was a lot of
thinking happening back then.

163
00:11:07,542 --> 00:11:10,420
Mmm. I'm glad we put a stop to that.

164
00:11:10,503 --> 00:11:11,504
Please, have a seat.

165
00:11:12,464 --> 00:11:14,257
So, I've gone over the numbers

166
00:11:14,341 --> 00:11:17,219
of the proposed agreement
of steel with Beijing

167
00:11:17,302 --> 00:11:19,387
and I have a couple
of questions for you.

168
00:11:19,471 --> 00:11:21,306
Madam President, we need
to evacuate you now.

169
00:11:21,389 --> 00:11:23,350
- What's going on?
- Please, Madam President. It's urgent.

170
00:11:23,433 --> 00:11:24,476
Ma'am.

171
00:11:26,936 --> 00:11:28,187
Where are you taking me?

172
00:11:28,271 --> 00:11:30,648
- We're moving you to the PEOC.
- Why?

173
00:11:30,732 --> 00:11:33,943
- They'll brief you down below, ma'am.
- Where's Francis?

174
00:11:55,798 --> 00:11:57,585
Where's Doug Stamper? And Mr. Yates?

175
00:11:57,597 --> 00:11:59,302
We're following protocol, ma'am.

176
00:11:59,386 --> 00:12:02,221
National Security Advisor
Cafferty is on her way.

177
00:12:03,515 --> 00:12:05,683
- Ma'am?
- No, we'll wait for Francis.

178
00:12:05,767 --> 00:12:06,684
He'll meet you inside.

179
00:12:06,768 --> 00:12:08,728
We will wait for Francis.
That's an order.

180
00:12:08,811 --> 00:12:10,647
- Madam President.
- Miss Cafferty, what's going on?

181
00:12:10,730 --> 00:12:11,898
Nothing's confirmed yet,

182
00:12:11,985 --> 00:12:15,204
but a truck carrying radioactive
material has gone missing.

183
00:12:18,112 --> 00:12:20,907
- Is this real?
- We have to talk to Green.

184
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:22,659
Let's head inside.

185
00:12:58,986 --> 00:13:00,071
Yes.

186
00:13:03,325 --> 00:13:05,618
Mmm-hmm.

187
00:13:06,202 --> 00:13:08,996
I see. Thank you.

188
00:13:11,123 --> 00:13:13,250
Homeland received word from CYBERCOM

189
00:13:13,335 --> 00:13:16,588
that a truck carrying three
cesium-137 irradiators

190
00:13:16,671 --> 00:13:17,797
missed two checkpoints.

191
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:19,757
It was supposed to be
traveling from Atlanta

192
00:13:19,841 --> 00:13:21,884
back to the manufacturer in Baltimore.

193
00:13:21,968 --> 00:13:24,846
- Where do we think the truck is now?
- Truck's GPS is offline.

194
00:13:24,929 --> 00:13:26,389
How the hell does a
thing like that happen?

195
00:13:26,473 --> 00:13:28,558
- We'll have to reevaluate.
- You're damn right we will.

196
00:13:28,641 --> 00:13:30,184
But we need to make some decisions.

197
00:13:30,267 --> 00:13:32,854
We should notify Metro PD
and Virginia State Police.

198
00:13:32,937 --> 00:13:34,564
Are we gonna evacuate the public?

199
00:13:34,647 --> 00:13:35,823
No. Before we do anything, I wanna

200
00:13:35,835 --> 00:13:37,233
speak to the head of counterterrorism.

201
00:13:37,316 --> 00:13:39,068
Get Assistant Director
Green on the line.

202
00:13:39,151 --> 00:13:41,716
- Ma'am, Homeland is over...
- The president is right.

203
00:13:42,822 --> 00:13:43,865
Ma'am?

204
00:13:45,533 --> 00:13:46,784
This is President Underwood.

205
00:13:46,868 --> 00:13:48,995
<i>At this time, we have
no idea who's responsible.</i>

206
00:13:49,070 --> 00:13:50,733
Director Green, perhaps it's better

207
00:13:50,758 --> 00:13:52,404
I patch you into the whole room.
One second.

208
00:13:55,251 --> 00:13:58,295
<i>The driver's been unreachable
since his shift began.</i>

209
00:13:58,380 --> 00:14:02,049
<i>There's enough radiation on that
truck to impact a 30-mile radius.</i>

210
00:14:02,133 --> 00:14:04,469
<i>Even if it's not weaponized,
it would be in the air,</i>

211
00:14:04,552 --> 00:14:07,304
<i>in the water, children, people...</i>

212
00:14:08,512 --> 00:14:12,619
General, I can hear the
wheels grinding from here.

213
00:14:12,644 --> 00:14:14,311
I'd rather not speculate, sir.

214
00:14:15,772 --> 00:14:17,356
Oh, please do.

215
00:14:19,233 --> 00:14:22,487
Over the past several days, there
has been increased ICO chatter,

216
00:14:22,570 --> 00:14:24,280
but that is the new normal.

217
00:14:26,010 --> 00:14:29,597
<i>We've sent over stats and
maps of potentially affected areas.</i>

218
00:14:42,674 --> 00:14:45,552
I don't know what's worse. A
dirty bomb about to go off

219
00:14:45,635 --> 00:14:48,179
or what'll happen to the city when
they know we're looking for one.

220
00:14:48,262 --> 00:14:51,933
- Who do we have left upstairs?
- Seth and LeAnn.

221
00:14:52,016 --> 00:14:53,560
You stay in touch with Green.

222
00:14:54,477 --> 00:14:58,898
If this is a dirty bomb, then we've
just entered a different world.

223
00:14:58,981 --> 00:15:00,024
Yes, sir.

224
00:15:01,484 --> 00:15:03,075
All right, we need to stay focused on

225
00:15:03,087 --> 00:15:04,821
our contingency plan for an evacuation

226
00:15:04,904 --> 00:15:07,114
without the appearance of doing so.

227
00:15:11,536 --> 00:15:13,204
We need to be ready to
implement one way...

228
00:15:13,287 --> 00:15:15,206
We need to get the cleanup
team from the Energy...

229
00:15:15,289 --> 00:15:17,875
...whose jurisdiction it is
to get the security cams...

230
00:15:21,045 --> 00:15:23,735
<i>Yes. Whenever it happens,
this appointment</i>

231
00:15:23,747 --> 00:15:25,883
<i>would break the court's deadlock.</i>

232
00:15:25,967 --> 00:15:28,260
<i>And we would get this
election going again.</i>

233
00:15:28,344 --> 00:15:30,555
<i>But let's step back a minute.</i>

234
00:15:30,638 --> 00:15:33,683
<i>Tennessee is out of the equation.</i>

235
00:15:33,766 --> 00:15:36,978
<i>Whoever wins that
state, it's not enough.</i>

236
00:15:37,061 --> 00:15:40,815
<i>It's come down to one state. Ohio.</i>

237
00:15:41,524 --> 00:15:44,491
<i>One state is about to choose the next</i>

238
00:15:44,503 --> 00:15:47,321
<i>President of these United States.</i>

239
00:15:47,404 --> 00:15:49,198
<i>How did we let this happen?</i>

240
00:15:49,727 --> 00:15:51,771
<i>And it keeps happening.</i>

241
00:15:51,909 --> 00:15:55,497
<i>This is an administration that
operates behind closed doors,</i>

242
00:15:55,580 --> 00:15:57,790
<i>out of the public eye.</i>

243
00:15:57,874 --> 00:16:00,332
<i>Today's sudden postponement is typical.</i>

244
00:16:00,402 --> 00:16:03,062
<i>With no announcement
in the Rose Garden,</i>

245
00:16:03,087 --> 00:16:06,508
<i>and literally zero news
coming from the White House,</i>

246
00:16:06,591 --> 00:16:09,426
<i>one has to wonder what is
going on behind the scenes</i>

247
00:16:09,511 --> 00:16:12,138
<i>to cause this unexpected delay.</i>

248
00:16:12,221 --> 00:16:14,932
<i>The silence is deafening.</i>

249
00:16:15,016 --> 00:16:20,229
<i>After such a protracted, confusing
and, frankly, chaotic election,</i>

250
00:16:20,312 --> 00:16:22,439
<i>we deserve clarity.</i>

251
00:16:22,524 --> 00:16:25,151
<i>Instead, here we are again...</i>

252
00:16:25,467 --> 00:16:28,738
<i>left out of the loop and
on the edge of our seats.</i>

253
00:16:29,147 --> 00:16:32,158
<i>I just hope America isn't
getting used to this.</i>

254
00:16:35,119 --> 00:16:37,705
- Hello?
<i>- Hey, it's me.</i>

255
00:16:37,789 --> 00:16:38,956
Doug?

256
00:16:39,040 --> 00:16:40,332
<i>Why wasn't I read in?</i>

257
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:43,711
- To what?
- Whatever's going on.

258
00:16:43,795 --> 00:16:46,714
If this is gonna play for us,
the president in the bunker,

259
00:16:46,798 --> 00:16:48,215
I need to know how to play it.

260
00:16:48,540 --> 00:16:51,752
There's a truck carrying radioactive
material that's gone missing.

261
00:16:52,595 --> 00:16:55,515
Okay. Should Seth and I
prepare a statement?

262
00:16:55,598 --> 00:16:58,475
- Where are we saying the truck is?
<i>- We don't know.</i>

263
00:16:59,393 --> 00:17:01,979
- When are we gonna find it?
- We don't know.

264
00:17:03,022 --> 00:17:05,692
<i>Wait, is something really happening?</i>

265
00:17:06,651 --> 00:17:07,694
Probably not.

266
00:17:13,074 --> 00:17:15,284
- Hello?
<i>- Probably not?</i>

267
00:17:15,367 --> 00:17:16,578
What am I supposed to do?

268
00:17:17,494 --> 00:17:18,705
- Is that Doug?
- Yeah.

269
00:17:18,788 --> 00:17:20,331
Can I talk to him?

270
00:17:20,414 --> 00:17:22,542
- Hey, what can you tell us?
<i>- Act normal.</i>

271
00:17:22,625 --> 00:17:25,712
Stay on point. Comment only
on the ongoing campaign.

272
00:17:25,795 --> 00:17:27,589
<i>I've already postponed
their scheduled events.</i>

273
00:17:27,672 --> 00:17:29,966
<i>Look, are we in danger here or what?</i>

274
00:17:30,967 --> 00:17:32,301
I can't answer.

275
00:17:33,260 --> 00:17:34,887
Because I don't know.

276
00:17:35,185 --> 00:17:38,146
<i>Await further instructions
from Homeland.</i>

277
00:17:38,171 --> 00:17:39,172
All right.

278
00:17:40,893 --> 00:17:42,729
Doug, should we be here?

279
00:17:44,938 --> 00:17:45,939
He hung up.

280
00:17:48,818 --> 00:17:50,236
What are we doing?

281
00:17:59,536 --> 00:18:01,664
Nora thinks we need to
notify Speaker McCarthy.

282
00:18:01,748 --> 00:18:03,791
I think it's too soon for a
continuity of government.

283
00:18:03,875 --> 00:18:06,335
If we're planning an evacuation,
Congress needs to be notified...

284
00:18:06,418 --> 00:18:08,963
I said, I believe it is a bit too early.

285
00:18:09,046 --> 00:18:11,132
Madam President, Director
Morrison thinks that...

286
00:18:11,215 --> 00:18:12,800
Wait a minute. Where is
Director Morrison? Why...

287
00:18:12,884 --> 00:18:15,552
She opted to stay at ODNI.
She's monitoring from there.

288
00:18:15,637 --> 00:18:17,388
Well, at least let's
get her on the phone.

289
00:18:17,471 --> 00:18:18,640
We should have wiped out ICO months ago

290
00:18:18,665 --> 00:18:19,573
when we had the chance.

291
00:18:19,598 --> 00:18:22,184
We didn't ask for your
personal opinion, General.

292
00:18:23,102 --> 00:18:26,022
What we need is an update on
the Ahmed Al Ahmadi situation.

293
00:18:26,441 --> 00:18:28,485
Yes, ma'am. I'll check with
Director Morrison now.

294
00:18:36,949 --> 00:18:38,367
I have contacts, you know.

295
00:18:39,451 --> 00:18:42,371
Private contractors in the
region that might be of help.

296
00:18:42,454 --> 00:18:44,534
Are you suggesting that your contacts

297
00:18:44,546 --> 00:18:46,751
know more than the Bureau, the NSA...

298
00:18:46,834 --> 00:18:48,502
I'm not suggesting anything.

299
00:18:49,545 --> 00:18:51,255
I'm telling you.

300
00:18:51,339 --> 00:18:54,508
I know third parties that have
negotiated with ICO in the past.

301
00:18:56,052 --> 00:18:59,639
Hostages and whatnot...
who may know something.

302
00:18:59,722 --> 00:19:01,307
But I need a line.

303
00:19:03,059 --> 00:19:04,727
Just a... a secure one.

304
00:19:07,980 --> 00:19:09,857
I can barely breathe in here.

305
00:19:11,025 --> 00:19:13,402
I'm gonna go get us a cup of coffee.

306
00:19:19,867 --> 00:19:23,079
How does Miss Davis have
this level of clearance?

307
00:19:25,581 --> 00:19:27,041
That's a good question.

308
00:19:36,801 --> 00:19:39,220
- Did we bring this on ourselves?
- What?

309
00:19:40,596 --> 00:19:42,556
- I'm sorry. I shouldn't have.
- Listen to me.

310
00:19:42,639 --> 00:19:46,811
Everything we've done, everything,
is exactly what we had to do.

311
00:19:48,980 --> 00:19:51,065
We don't even know if this is real.

312
00:20:22,764 --> 00:20:24,431
I get these in Hong Kong.

313
00:20:25,767 --> 00:20:29,061
The best instant coffee comes
out of the Pacific Rim.

314
00:20:32,356 --> 00:20:35,026
- Would you like one?
- If you can spare it.

315
00:20:35,943 --> 00:20:38,237
Oh, I always have three
or four in my bag.

316
00:20:44,701 --> 00:20:47,163
I wonder how
long we'll be down here.

317
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:49,874
The situation's still unclear.

318
00:20:52,919 --> 00:20:55,838
I shouldn't be drinking coffee.
I still feel a little shaky.

319
00:21:00,467 --> 00:21:01,761
You don't look it.

320
00:21:12,271 --> 00:21:13,522
Feel my pulse.

321
00:21:18,652 --> 00:21:20,863
You seem very much in control to me.

322
00:21:27,829 --> 00:21:29,038
So do you.

323
00:21:31,123 --> 00:21:33,042
What does that say about the two of us?

324
00:21:46,848 --> 00:21:47,974
Hmm.

325
00:21:56,023 --> 00:21:57,399
Yes, thank you.

326
00:21:58,525 --> 00:22:00,777
The SEAL team is on the
trail of Ahmed Al Ahmadi,

327
00:22:00,862 --> 00:22:02,448
but National Intelligence believes

328
00:22:02,460 --> 00:22:04,198
he's discovered we're following him

329
00:22:04,281 --> 00:22:06,408
and the truck is a countermeasure.

330
00:22:06,492 --> 00:22:10,121
ICO wants to see Ahmadi walking
out of Damascus in one piece.

331
00:22:10,204 --> 00:22:12,373
If we strike, they will hit back.

332
00:22:12,456 --> 00:22:14,250
Evacuation procedures
need to be initiated...

333
00:22:14,333 --> 00:22:16,002
- Just hold on!
- No, the public is our priority...

334
00:22:16,085 --> 00:22:18,420
Hold on! I want to know how
close we are to a strike

335
00:22:18,504 --> 00:22:21,423
and where this goddamn truck is
before we make any final decisions.

336
00:22:21,507 --> 00:22:22,579
"We make any decisions"?

337
00:22:22,591 --> 00:22:24,426
Yes, I am still in a
position to make...

338
00:22:24,510 --> 00:22:26,845
Correct me if I'm wrong, but
you are not in a position...

339
00:22:26,929 --> 00:22:29,974
Nora. The enemy isn't in here.

340
00:22:36,188 --> 00:22:38,370
Cafferty is right. We should evacuate.

341
00:22:38,780 --> 00:22:41,090
But it's the general who's on my mind.

342
00:22:42,028 --> 00:22:43,279
Miss Cafferty.

343
00:22:43,362 --> 00:22:46,657
I was entirely out of line.
Please accept my apology.

344
00:22:52,079 --> 00:22:53,205
<i>I spoke with Davis.</i>

345
00:22:53,289 --> 00:22:56,625
- And?
- Nothing. She was just flexing.

346
00:22:59,753 --> 00:23:00,922
Cathy.

347
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:13,350
Who called a meeting with Claire today?
You or Miss Davis?

348
00:23:13,434 --> 00:23:14,518
Jane did.

349
00:23:15,644 --> 00:23:17,021
Thank you very much, Cathy.

350
00:23:17,104 --> 00:23:18,689
- Was that all?
- Yes, thank you.

351
00:23:19,648 --> 00:23:20,983
Oh, sorry, one more thing.

352
00:23:21,067 --> 00:23:25,154
When did Braegher get his fourth star?
Which administration?

353
00:23:25,237 --> 00:23:26,863
A couple back.

354
00:23:26,948 --> 00:23:28,699
So he and Brockhart together?

355
00:23:29,408 --> 00:23:32,286
And a few others who were elevated
around the same time, yes.

356
00:23:32,954 --> 00:23:34,121
Thank you, Cathy.

357
00:23:40,877 --> 00:23:43,547
That Brockhart spot we talked about.
You have it?

358
00:23:44,548 --> 00:23:45,674
Is it verified?

359
00:23:46,592 --> 00:23:48,135
Hold on.

360
00:23:52,098 --> 00:23:54,391
Ready.

361
00:23:56,268 --> 00:23:57,436
<i>I swear to God,</i>

362
00:23:57,519 --> 00:23:59,230
<i>if Underwood puts soldiers
on those borders,</i>

363
00:23:59,313 --> 00:24:01,565
<i>I'll be the first to
tell them not to listen.</i>

364
00:24:01,648 --> 00:24:04,776
<i>If the President of the United
States gives orders like that,</i>

365
00:24:04,860 --> 00:24:06,612
<i>you put him out of his misery.</i>

366
00:24:06,695 --> 00:24:08,489
<i>That's it. That's all I have.</i>

367
00:24:09,490 --> 00:24:11,367
No, that's good.

368
00:24:11,450 --> 00:24:12,994
<i>If we survive the day.</i>

369
00:24:13,077 --> 00:24:14,996
<i>Is Seth still in the office with you?</i>

370
00:24:15,079 --> 00:24:18,790
I'm in the Oval, sitting
behind the Resolute desk.

371
00:24:18,874 --> 00:24:21,293
<i>That's not you.</i>

372
00:24:21,377 --> 00:24:26,132
You know, you keep deciding who I
am and you keep reading me wrong.

373
00:24:26,215 --> 00:24:28,550
<i>Are there rumors about
what's going on down here?</i>

374
00:24:28,634 --> 00:24:30,677
Yes, but we're deflecting.

375
00:24:30,761 --> 00:24:33,930
- Has the Conway campaign reached out?
<i>- Not yet.</i>

376
00:24:34,015 --> 00:24:37,726
The general's on a stump in Ohio
and the governor's off the grid.

377
00:24:37,809 --> 00:24:40,937
<i>- Okay. Stay on him.</i>
- I will.

378
00:24:41,022 --> 00:24:43,857
Unless it's the end of the
world and it doesn't matter.

379
00:24:45,275 --> 00:24:47,069
Goodbye, Doug Stamper.

380
00:24:52,783 --> 00:24:55,577
Are you sure you should
be in there, Goldilocks?

381
00:25:35,951 --> 00:25:37,078
Are you all right?

382
00:25:39,663 --> 00:25:42,749
Honestly, I was thinking
about how far down we are

383
00:25:42,833 --> 00:25:44,251
and how it's not my favorite thing.

384
00:25:46,087 --> 00:25:48,130
I... I'm sorry. Do... do
you need to be in here?

385
00:25:48,214 --> 00:25:49,506
No. No, no. It's fine.

386
00:25:50,966 --> 00:25:53,594
I used to have a fear of
flying, but I got over it.

387
00:25:54,511 --> 00:25:56,430
Doesn't bother me at all anymore.

388
00:25:57,431 --> 00:26:00,392
But the pendulum seems to
have swung the other way.

389
00:26:01,102 --> 00:26:03,812
If I think too hard, I
start to feel buried.

390
00:26:03,895 --> 00:26:07,399
Forgive me. It's the recirculated
air, makes things worse.

391
00:26:10,319 --> 00:26:13,447
Miss Davis, why are you here?

392
00:26:13,530 --> 00:26:15,301
This is where the
Secret Service led me.

393
00:26:15,313 --> 00:26:15,907
No.

394
00:26:16,533 --> 00:26:19,953
Access list or not, you
have to choose to be here.

395
00:26:20,036 --> 00:26:23,249
- I always choose the safest place.
- Why are you here?

396
00:26:26,001 --> 00:26:28,170
It felt like an opportunity.

397
00:26:28,754 --> 00:26:31,632
A chance for a meeting,
not quite on the books.

398
00:26:31,715 --> 00:26:34,760
I just got off the
phone, Madam President.

399
00:26:34,843 --> 00:26:38,180
I have information from abroad,
from private contractors...

400
00:26:38,264 --> 00:26:40,641
Ahmadi is in Damascus.

401
00:26:40,724 --> 00:26:44,102
And a number of parties
were racing to capture him,

402
00:26:44,186 --> 00:26:46,730
including, of course, the United States.

403
00:26:46,813 --> 00:26:48,190
But no one...

404
00:26:49,275 --> 00:26:51,818
will be capturing him today.

405
00:26:52,611 --> 00:26:54,363
Or before the election.

406
00:26:55,614 --> 00:26:57,032
I've made a career...

407
00:26:58,033 --> 00:27:00,786
out of dealing with problematic
parts of the world.

408
00:27:04,039 --> 00:27:08,585
It's kind of my vocation to
imagine the unimaginable.

409
00:27:13,340 --> 00:27:14,508
Excuse me.

410
00:27:21,723 --> 00:27:23,225
- Pardon me.
- I'm sorry.

411
00:27:23,309 --> 00:27:25,352
- It's all right.
- Excuse me, Mr. President.

412
00:27:31,608 --> 00:27:35,529
I had the distinct feeling she
was offering Ahmadi to us.

413
00:27:35,612 --> 00:27:36,780
Meaning?

414
00:27:36,863 --> 00:27:39,533
She said there are a number of
groups looking to capture him,

415
00:27:39,616 --> 00:27:43,495
but that no one will. Not
today or before the election.

416
00:27:45,163 --> 00:27:46,873
We brought this on ourselves.

417
00:27:47,791 --> 00:27:50,211
- We pushed too hard.
- We've survived.

418
00:27:50,294 --> 00:27:53,464
- We isolated ourselves, Francis.
- So what?

419
00:27:53,547 --> 00:27:56,425
We both know something the rest of
the world refuses to acknowledge.

420
00:27:56,508 --> 00:27:59,595
There is no justice, only conquest.

421
00:27:59,678 --> 00:28:02,264
And let me tell you, we
let them evacuate D.C.,

422
00:28:02,348 --> 00:28:04,850
we are done, Claire. We've lost.

423
00:28:04,933 --> 00:28:06,435
Yes?

424
00:28:10,856 --> 00:28:14,443
I just spoke to LeAnn.
You need to hear this.

425
00:28:14,526 --> 00:28:15,902
<i>I swear to God,</i>

426
00:28:15,986 --> 00:28:17,738
<i>if Underwood puts soldiers
on those borders,</i>

427
00:28:17,821 --> 00:28:19,948
<i>I'll be the first to
tell them not to listen.</i>

428
00:28:20,031 --> 00:28:23,034
<i>If the President of the United
States gives orders like that,</i>

429
00:28:23,118 --> 00:28:24,786
<i>you put him out of his misery.</i>

430
00:28:31,293 --> 00:28:32,294
Let me out.

431
00:28:32,378 --> 00:28:34,796
- I'm sorry, sir. I'm not allowed...
- Open the door.

432
00:28:34,880 --> 00:28:37,173
- My orders are to...
- I am no longer the president.

433
00:28:37,258 --> 00:28:40,427
I have no responsibilities or
obligations. Isn't that correct?

434
00:28:40,511 --> 00:28:42,221
We can't send you above until
the threat is contained...

435
00:28:42,304 --> 00:28:45,181
- Open this door.
- Let him out.

436
00:28:45,266 --> 00:28:47,893
- Ma'am?
- Let the president out.

437
00:28:50,145 --> 00:28:51,230
Open the door.

438
00:28:54,107 --> 00:28:55,108
Open it.

439
00:30:21,445 --> 00:30:23,113
Ma'am.

440
00:30:23,196 --> 00:30:25,441
We need to initiate evacuation now.

441
00:30:25,453 --> 00:30:28,076
No, General. We'll
do it when I say so.

442
00:30:35,208 --> 00:30:36,460
I'm really sorry.

443
00:30:36,543 --> 00:30:39,546
I know I agreed to do this, but
I have to go pick up my kids.

444
00:30:40,130 --> 00:30:42,173
Okay. Well, what if I just
rode in the car with you?

445
00:30:42,257 --> 00:30:44,134
You know, parents are
texting one another.

446
00:30:44,217 --> 00:30:46,218
One of them works at the NSA and he

447
00:30:46,230 --> 00:30:48,472
thinks there's a terror threat, so...

448
00:30:48,555 --> 00:30:51,767
I mean, this has happened before,
but you just... You never know.

449
00:30:51,850 --> 00:30:55,103
My mom died of kidney
failure last month.

450
00:30:55,506 --> 00:30:57,592
Oh, I'm so sorry.

451
00:30:58,482 --> 00:31:00,256
Uh, was she on the donor list?

452
00:31:00,268 --> 00:31:02,611
Yeah, but not close
enough to the top.

453
00:31:04,112 --> 00:31:06,782
Do you mind? You could talk
while we walk out of here.

454
00:31:07,991 --> 00:31:10,869
Um... sure. Yeah.

455
00:31:12,078 --> 00:31:15,081
Uh, how long was Anthony sick for?

456
00:31:15,999 --> 00:31:19,628
Uh... about two years.

457
00:31:21,547 --> 00:31:25,592
And he fought it hard. So hard.
The entire way.

458
00:31:28,970 --> 00:31:33,559
This unit, if they pay cash,
I don't ask questions.

459
00:31:33,642 --> 00:31:36,603
- But you remember these young women?
- Yeah, of course.

460
00:31:36,687 --> 00:31:40,023
They were very close, if
you know what I mean.

461
00:31:40,106 --> 00:31:41,692
But they were sweet.

462
00:31:43,402 --> 00:31:46,655
And did you ever see... this man?

463
00:31:48,782 --> 00:31:50,701
Look, I don't know what
was going on here.

464
00:31:50,784 --> 00:31:52,453
But you recognize him?

465
00:31:54,413 --> 00:31:56,832
Yeah. Okay?

466
00:31:56,915 --> 00:32:00,836
Someone looking like him paid the rent.
Three months, up-front.

467
00:32:00,919 --> 00:32:03,046
But like I said, I don't judge.

468
00:32:08,885 --> 00:32:12,013
I'm not sure what you're asking, Mr.
President.

469
00:32:12,097 --> 00:32:13,474
Oh, please.

470
00:32:14,641 --> 00:32:17,853
Someone or someones...

471
00:32:17,936 --> 00:32:20,439
tried to make my wife
and I lose the election

472
00:32:20,522 --> 00:32:23,191
by keeping us underground today.

473
00:32:23,274 --> 00:32:26,612
And I would like to know
what you know about that.

474
00:32:26,695 --> 00:32:28,614
We've all been responding in real

475
00:32:28,626 --> 00:32:30,907
time to a potential terrorist attack.

476
00:32:30,991 --> 00:32:34,536
But you chose to stay here. Why
weren't you in the bunker with us?

477
00:32:34,620 --> 00:32:36,830
I chose to remain in my office

478
00:32:36,913 --> 00:32:39,750
to oversee the capture or
killing of one Ahmed Al Ahmadi.

479
00:32:40,333 --> 00:32:41,334
Mmm.

480
00:32:41,417 --> 00:32:43,629
And yet there was great
tension this morning

481
00:32:43,712 --> 00:32:45,421
between you and General Braegher.

482
00:32:45,506 --> 00:32:47,257
Difference in approach.

483
00:32:47,841 --> 00:32:50,844
We are not going to evacuate
the District of Columbia.

484
00:32:50,927 --> 00:32:54,347
I want you to understand that.
Come what may.

485
00:32:56,767 --> 00:33:00,646
And I promise you this... Vanessa.

486
00:33:02,105 --> 00:33:04,912
When I find out exactly
what has happened,

487
00:33:04,924 --> 00:33:07,611
I'm going to remember
this conversation,

488
00:33:07,694 --> 00:33:10,489
when you chose to withhold information.

489
00:33:11,865 --> 00:33:16,327
General Braegher is a strong
supporter of General Brockhart.

490
00:33:20,415 --> 00:33:21,958
Did they conspire?

491
00:33:26,379 --> 00:33:30,466
Did they use... terror...

492
00:33:30,551 --> 00:33:36,347
and this evacuation to
cost me this election?

493
00:33:37,516 --> 00:33:40,060
I'm not a fan of the general...

494
00:33:41,436 --> 00:33:45,816
but... that's a strong charge, and
there's no proof to support it.

495
00:33:46,900 --> 00:33:51,279
You know, what you
people protect best is each other.

496
00:33:51,863 --> 00:33:54,371
We lost Ahmadi a short time ago and

497
00:33:54,383 --> 00:33:57,118
believe he is no longer in Damascus.

498
00:33:58,453 --> 00:34:00,789
Of course.

499
00:34:02,415 --> 00:34:03,750
Of course.

500
00:34:09,339 --> 00:34:10,924
Now you listen to me...

501
00:34:12,467 --> 00:34:15,074
This was nothing more or less than

502
00:34:15,086 --> 00:34:18,014
an attempted coup, plain and simple.

503
00:34:18,682 --> 00:34:22,936
And I do not know to what degree
you have been directly involved.

504
00:34:23,019 --> 00:34:25,731
But you will resolve it.

505
00:34:26,522 --> 00:34:27,608
Now.

506
00:34:29,275 --> 00:34:31,277
Do I make myself clear?

507
00:34:34,823 --> 00:34:36,116
Yes, sir.

508
00:34:50,421 --> 00:34:52,924
The truck's been found.

509
00:34:53,008 --> 00:34:54,690
Now we can't know for sure, but it

510
00:34:54,702 --> 00:34:56,595
looks as though ICO wasn't involved.

511
00:34:56,678 --> 00:34:59,097
The irradiators and cesium
were accounted for.

512
00:34:59,180 --> 00:35:01,410
The truck was accidentally parked at

513
00:35:01,422 --> 00:35:03,727
a medical device factory in Durham.

514
00:35:03,810 --> 00:35:06,396
The plant foreman never reported it.

515
00:35:06,479 --> 00:35:08,899
So we can relax for now, at least.

516
00:35:08,982 --> 00:35:11,652
I just wanna thank you all
for your efforts. Thank you.

517
00:35:16,114 --> 00:35:19,575
Madam President. You'll have
my resignation in the morning.

518
00:35:20,160 --> 00:35:21,161
Nora...

519
00:35:22,287 --> 00:35:24,748
these were extraordinary
circumstances today.

520
00:35:24,831 --> 00:35:26,939
What would our administration be if we

521
00:35:26,951 --> 00:35:29,127
didn't allow for some human failings?

522
00:35:37,678 --> 00:35:40,221
Get the presser going.
We're coming up now.

523
00:35:40,305 --> 00:35:42,223
Concerning Ahmadi...

524
00:35:43,141 --> 00:35:44,893
We didn't find him.

525
00:35:44,976 --> 00:35:47,020
You will. You can.

526
00:35:47,103 --> 00:35:50,065
- What are you offering?
- Help.

527
00:35:50,148 --> 00:35:52,693
If you'd like it, Madam President.

528
00:36:00,951 --> 00:36:03,662
Can you elaborate
on the drill earlier today?

529
00:36:03,745 --> 00:36:05,413
Well, drills happen all the time.

530
00:36:05,496 --> 00:36:07,098
It's part of the
administration's ongoing

531
00:36:07,110 --> 00:36:08,416
efforts to keep the country safe.

532
00:36:08,499 --> 00:36:11,252
- Yes, but there's usually a warning.
- What's the point of that?

533
00:36:12,545 --> 00:36:14,798
Who's next?

534
00:36:27,393 --> 00:36:28,895
Did you look at the file?

535
00:36:30,105 --> 00:36:31,231
I didn't have to.

536
00:36:33,524 --> 00:36:37,653
I'll expect your signature on the
resignation letter within the hour.

537
00:36:39,239 --> 00:36:42,492
Unless you choose to implicate
whoever else was involved.

538
00:36:52,085 --> 00:36:54,587
You don't deserve to
be in the White House.

539
00:36:55,964 --> 00:36:57,799
Neither you nor your husband.

540
00:37:03,805 --> 00:37:06,266
I'd wish you the best, but I
don't think you'll need it.

541
00:37:06,349 --> 00:37:09,895
I'm fairly certain you'll do
very well in the private sector.

542
00:37:18,236 --> 00:37:21,156
I've scheduled a meeting with Jane
Davis for the end of the week.

543
00:37:21,239 --> 00:37:22,240
Good.

544
00:37:22,323 --> 00:37:24,075
Also, I was going to
mention this earlier,

545
00:37:24,159 --> 00:37:28,079
but Cathy's been very curious
about Aidan Macallan.

546
00:37:28,163 --> 00:37:30,040
I've thrown her off the scent, but...

547
00:37:30,123 --> 00:37:34,127
Cathy's not the problem.
The problem is Macallan,

548
00:37:34,210 --> 00:37:37,422
and the person who allowed
Macallan to become the problem.

549
00:37:42,593 --> 00:37:45,555
The foundation's raised over 80K.

550
00:37:45,638 --> 00:37:49,309
Anthony became status one on the
donor list on March 15th, 2016.

551
00:37:49,392 --> 00:37:52,270
Moretti talked about it as,
uh, the last day of her life

552
00:37:52,353 --> 00:37:53,438
before she corrected herself.

553
00:37:53,521 --> 00:37:55,065
Spent every spare second with the kids.

554
00:37:55,148 --> 00:37:57,442
They were building a go-kart.
They were pretty close to done.

555
00:37:57,525 --> 00:37:58,526
- Okay.
- I got more.

556
00:37:58,609 --> 00:38:00,904
- No, I got it.
- What were you looking for?

557
00:38:00,987 --> 00:38:02,322
It's nothing.

558
00:38:06,076 --> 00:38:08,286
- Okay.
- What?

559
00:38:08,369 --> 00:38:10,538
You wanna tell me what happened
in the White House today?

560
00:38:10,621 --> 00:38:13,208
No, I don't.

561
00:38:20,924 --> 00:38:22,550
All right, I've been
waiting to say something,

562
00:38:22,633 --> 00:38:25,053
but I've waited and I don't
want to wait anymore.

563
00:38:25,136 --> 00:38:27,931
Consider me for a job at
the White House, in comms.

564
00:38:31,267 --> 00:38:34,354
"Go get this. Find me that. I
need this." I'm tired of it.

565
00:38:34,437 --> 00:38:37,023
If you don't ask, you get asked.
That's what I'm starting to realize.

566
00:38:37,107 --> 00:38:38,191
I'll put a word in.

567
00:38:38,691 --> 00:38:40,066
Yeah? Well, what does that mean?

568
00:38:40,094 --> 00:38:42,721
It means that when the moment
is right, I'll mention you.

569
00:38:47,575 --> 00:38:50,203
<i>Yes, whenever it happens...</i>

570
00:38:50,286 --> 00:38:52,956
<i>this appointment would
break the court's deadlock</i>

571
00:38:53,039 --> 00:38:55,375
<i>and we would get this
election going again.</i>

572
00:38:55,458 --> 00:38:57,836
<i>But let's step back a minute...</i>

573
00:38:57,919 --> 00:39:00,255
<i>- Tennessee...</i>
- Where's your salt?

574
00:39:00,839 --> 00:39:03,424
<i>- Whoever wins that state...</i>
- Right side of the sink.

575
00:39:04,217 --> 00:39:07,262
<i>It's come down to one state:</i>

576
00:39:07,345 --> 00:39:08,471
<i>Ohio.</i>

577
00:39:08,555 --> 00:39:11,136
<i>One state is about to choose the next</i>

578
00:39:11,148 --> 00:39:13,601
<i>President of these United States.</i>

579
00:39:13,726 --> 00:39:16,312
- Was it really a drill?
- Hmm.

580
00:39:16,396 --> 00:39:19,941
<i>This is an administration that
operates behind closed doors.</i>

581
00:39:20,066 --> 00:39:22,527
You know, with everything
that was happening today,

582
00:39:22,610 --> 00:39:24,863
this reporter from the <i>Herald</i> came by.

583
00:39:25,780 --> 00:39:26,865
What?

584
00:39:26,948 --> 00:39:29,659
Wants to do a story on
Tony and the foundation.

585
00:39:35,498 --> 00:39:36,624
What was his name?

586
00:40:04,402 --> 00:40:07,322
Davis implied she could
help us track down Ahmadi.

587
00:40:07,405 --> 00:40:10,075
I think we should hear
what she has to say.

588
00:40:11,534 --> 00:40:14,120
She's got a quality
about her, doesn't she?

589
00:40:15,038 --> 00:40:17,248
Attractive and terrifying.

590
00:40:18,458 --> 00:40:21,586
Like the urge to pet a red tail fox.

591
00:40:26,591 --> 00:40:29,010
The general offered his letter?

592
00:40:29,094 --> 00:40:33,056
Uh, he did. And refused
to implicate anyone.

593
00:40:36,809 --> 00:40:40,605
You were right, Claire. We
need to sit down with Usher.

594
00:40:42,273 --> 00:40:45,986
Just so happens, he's going to
Northern California this weekend

595
00:40:46,069 --> 00:40:49,155
to meet with a group of men

596
00:40:49,239 --> 00:40:52,951
to discuss the crisis and
the future of our country.

597
00:40:53,034 --> 00:40:56,746
- Well, you need to be invited to that.
- Yes, let's get him in.

598
00:41:01,334 --> 00:41:04,712
I know it's obvious,
but it always strikes me.

599
00:41:04,795 --> 00:41:05,921
No women.

600
00:41:07,215 --> 00:41:09,217
Well, it was a different time.

601
00:41:12,012 --> 00:41:13,304
Terrible.

602
00:41:13,388 --> 00:41:16,599
The war or the restrictions of the era?

603
00:41:17,517 --> 00:41:18,726
Both.

604
00:41:18,809 --> 00:41:20,895
Well, you know my position.

605
00:41:21,812 --> 00:41:24,065
I'm all for women in combat.

606
00:43:07,543 --> 00:43:10,296
False alarm... hmm?

607
00:43:16,302 --> 00:43:17,970
I was worried about you.

608
00:43:40,493 --> 00:43:42,828
I worry about you all the time, Claire.

609
00:43:48,251 --> 00:43:51,671
But I know that's not the kind
of thing you like to hear.

610
00:44:12,900 --> 00:44:15,486
Mark. Come in.

611
00:44:16,404 --> 00:44:18,573
- We have much to discuss.
- Madam President.

612
00:44:19,490 --> 00:44:21,367
Uh, Mr. President.

613
00:44:22,117 --> 00:44:23,661
As I believe you know,

614
00:44:23,744 --> 00:44:27,957
yesterday we had something of a
drill here in the White House.

615
00:44:28,040 --> 00:44:30,460
I know people are wondering
what that was about.

616
00:44:30,543 --> 00:44:33,003
Yes. Everyone except you.

617
00:44:33,921 --> 00:44:36,257
The announcement of the recess
appointment of Judge Benson

618
00:44:36,341 --> 00:44:38,426
has been rescheduled
for tomorrow morning.

619
00:44:38,509 --> 00:44:40,261
Good. So...

620
00:44:41,679 --> 00:44:42,888
we have an election.

621
00:44:42,972 --> 00:44:45,496
Which you will not be able to win with

622
00:44:45,508 --> 00:44:47,977
another so-called October surprise.

623
00:44:48,060 --> 00:44:52,232
- Well, we are way past October.
- We certainly are.

624
00:44:54,650 --> 00:44:56,861
I understand Ahmed Al
Ahmadi is still a threat?

625
00:44:57,445 --> 00:45:00,906
Yes, but he's so elusive, as you know.

626
00:45:00,990 --> 00:45:03,284
It's a shame you weren't
able to capture him.

627
00:45:03,368 --> 00:45:04,994
Well...

628
00:45:05,077 --> 00:45:07,216
I believe that the opportunity will

629
00:45:07,228 --> 00:45:09,624
present itself to the next president,

630
00:45:09,707 --> 00:45:11,459
whomever he may be.

631
00:45:12,293 --> 00:45:14,044
If Will Conway wins the office,

632
00:45:14,128 --> 00:45:16,464
I can assure you that'll
be a top priority.

633
00:45:16,547 --> 00:45:17,548
Hmm.

634
00:45:18,466 --> 00:45:20,134
This terror has got to stop.

635
00:45:24,930 --> 00:45:26,682
I've taken enough of your time.

636
00:45:27,725 --> 00:45:30,077
Oh, Mark, I just want to play something

637
00:45:30,089 --> 00:45:32,272
for you. It'll only take a moment.

638
00:45:33,606 --> 00:45:34,774
<i>I swear to God,</i>

639
00:45:34,857 --> 00:45:36,817
<i>if Underwood puts soldiers
on those borders,</i>

640
00:45:36,901 --> 00:45:38,944
<i>I'll be the first to
tell them not to listen.</i>

641
00:45:39,028 --> 00:45:42,323
<i>If the President of the United
States gives orders like that,</i>

642
00:45:42,407 --> 00:45:43,324
<i>you put him out of his...</i>

643
00:45:43,408 --> 00:45:45,660
Okay. I don't need to hear anymore.

644
00:45:45,743 --> 00:45:47,161
Oh, but, Mark...

645
00:45:47,244 --> 00:45:49,204
it gets so much better.

